    note:'All AM dosing preferred. NAD+ may cause flushing — always start LOW. Add each peptide one week apart to isolate reactions.',
    studies:[{title:'NAD+ and Aging: Therapeutic Review',journal:'Cell Metabolism 2018',summary:'Established NAD+ as longevity intervention target.',pmid:'29719682',url:'https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29719682/'}],
    plainEnglish:`Think of your mitochondria as the building's power plant — and imagine it's been failing through four completely separate problems at once.\n\nThe fuel supply is running low. The generator membranes have corroded. The fuel conversion process has become inefficient. And there's an enzyme actively sabotaging the fuel supply that nobody's dealt with yet.\n\nThis stack sends four separate repair teams into the power plant simultaneously.\n\n**NAD+ — The Fuel Delivery**\n\nThe essential molecule that powers the entire mitochondrial energy cycle. Levels drop roughly 50% between age 20 and 50. Everything downstream suffers when the fuel runs critically low. This is the delivery that has to happen first.\n\n**SS-31 — The Generator Shield**\n\nThe inner mitochondrial membrane is where energy gets produced — and where oxidative stress does the most damage. SS-31 sits directly on that membrane and acts as a protective lining, reducing the corrosion that accumulates over time.\n\n**MOTS-c — The Efficiency Upgrade**\n\nA peptide produced by the mitochondria themselves. It activates AMPK — the same metabolic switch your body flips during cardio. Better fat burning, better insulin response. The generators produce more output per unit of fuel.\n\n**5-amino-1mq — Removing the Saboteur**\n\nNNMT is an enzyme that breaks down NAD+ and signals fat cells to stay expanded. 5-amino-1mq locks it out — keeping the fuel supply higher for longer and making everything else's job easier.\n\n| Compound | Role |\n|---|---|\n| NAD+ | Restores the fuel supply the generators have been running low on |\n| SS-31 | Shields the inner generator membrane from oxidative corrosion |\n| MOTS-c | Upgrades fuel conversion efficiency — the exercise-mimicking switch |\n| 5-amino-1mq | Locks out the enzyme sabotaging the fuel supply |\n\n---\n\nFour failure modes, four repair teams. You can't restore the power plant by fixing only one of them. All four running simultaneously is what actually brings it back to full capacity.`,
