    plainEnglish:`Think of this as the most comprehensive renovation project on the list — four crews, four completely different problems, one building.\n\nThe blueprint room needs resetting. Specific sections need local repair. The entire structural framework needs maintenance. And there's a slow fire burning through the walls — chronic inflammation — that nobody's put out yet. You can't fully renovate a building while that fire is still spreading.\n\nThis stack sends all four crews in simultaneously.\n\n**GHK-Cu — The Blueprint Reset**\n\nGoes into the blueprint room and resets gene expression back toward renewal — collagen, elastin, cellular regeneration. The building's instructions get restored before the renovation begins.\n\n**BPC-157 — The Local Repair Crew**\n\nShows up at the specific damage addresses — gut lining, injured tissue, inflamed areas — and runs new blood supply lines so repair materials can actually reach the site. Local damage requires a local crew.\n\n**TB-500 — The Structural Engineer**\n\nWhile BPC-157 handles specific locations, TB-500 works on the entire building's structural framework simultaneously — regulating actin throughout the body, reducing scarring, improving flexibility everywhere at once.\n\n**KPV — The Fire Suppression Crew**\n\nKPV directly inhibits NF-kB — the master regulator of inflammation. The slow fire burning through the walls that's been draining every other crew's resources. Particularly effective at mucosal surfaces: gut lining, colon, IBD. KPV goes into the walls and actually puts it out.\n\n| Compound | Role |\n|---|---|\n| GHK-Cu | Blueprint reset — collagen and cellular renewal instructions restored |\n| BPC-157 | Local repair crew — supply lines run to the specific damage sites |\n| TB-500 | Structural engineer — whole-building framework maintenance |\n| KPV | Fire suppression crew — shuts down the NF-kB inflammatory fire |\n\n---\n\nYou can't renovate a building while it's on fire. KPV puts the fire out. BPC-157 repairs the damage. TB-500 keeps the structure sound. GHK-Cu restores the blueprints. Every crew doing a completely different job at the same time.`,
