    plainEnglish:`Think of the hormonal transition as a building changing its primary operating mode — from one function to another.\n\nThe core infrastructure runs continuously through both phases. But there are two distinct stages, and each requires a different specialty crew to handle the phase-specific work. The foundation team doesn't change. The specialty contractor does.\n\n**CJC-1295 + Ipamorelin — The Core Infrastructure (Both Phases)**\n\nGH declines alongside estrogen. These two keep the overnight foreman on site — maintaining muscle, sleep quality, and body composition throughout the entire transition. The dispatch memo and the direct call, running continuously regardless of phase.\n\n**BPC-157 — The Maintenance Crew (Both Phases)**\n\nJoint inflammation and gut permeability are the most overlooked complaints in both perimenopause and post-menopause. BPC-157 keeps the local repair crews active through both phases — running supply lines to joints, maintaining the gut lining, addressing the day-to-day wear continuously.\n\n**Kisspeptin-10 — The Perimenopause Specialist**\n\nIn perimenopause, the building's hormonal signaling system starts sending erratic orders — the ovaries are still active but inconsistent, and LH/FSH levels fluctuate unpredictably. Kisspeptin-10 smooths that signaling from headquarters, bringing order to the chain of command while the ovaries can still respond. Only runs while the ovaries are active.\n\n**Epithalon — The Post-Menopause Specialist**\n\nOnce the ovaries go offline, Kisspeptin's job is done. The specialty contractor changes. Epithalon takes over — going into the foundation and reinforcing the telomere caps, shifting focus from hormonal signaling to deep structural longevity work. Burst cycles only: 10–20 days, a few times per year.\n\n| Compound | Role |\n|---|---|\n| CJC-1295 (no DAC) | Core infrastructure — overnight foreman scheduled through both phases |\n| Ipamorelin | Core infrastructure — direct call ensuring the foreman shows up |\n| BPC-157 | Maintenance crew — joints and gut lining through both phases |\n| Kisspeptin-10 | Perimenopause specialist — smooths erratic ovarian signaling |\n| Epithalon | Post-menopause specialist — telomere foundation reinforcement |\n\n---\n\nThe core infrastructure runs continuously. The specialty crew adapts when the phase changes. HRT remains the clinical foundation — these peptides address what HRT doesn't cover.`,
